course: dictionary
lesson: 4553
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word heaven is a good example. «The Bible pictures heaven as a city of gold» means a holy place where God lives. «This cake is heaven!» means the cake is very, very nice, not that it has gone to a holy place.
explain: Look at the words around it to pick the right meaning. Words like God, Bible, or after they die point to the religious meaning. Words like cake, lovely, or yummy point to the meaning "very pleasant". Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some words belong to set phrases, and the whole phrase has its own meaning. «Heaven knows» does not mean the sky knows something. It means nobody knows. «Thank heavens!» shows relief, not a prayer. Learn the phrase as one chunk.
fact: Heaven is a noun. Heavens is also a noun. Heaven with a capital letter is the name of the holy place in many religions.
fact: In many religions, heaven is the place where God or gods live, and where good people are believed to go after they die.
fact: «Heaven» can also mean a very happy or pleasant place or state, as in «this cake is heaven!»
fact: Old or poetic writing uses «the heavens» to mean the sky.
fact: «Heaven knows» means nobody knows. «In seventh heaven» means very happy.
exercise: «The Bible pictures heaven as a city of gold.» In this sentence, what does heaven mean? | *A holy place where God lives | A very pleasant state, like a lovely holiday | A kind of cake | The sky, high above the clouds
exercise: «This cake is heaven!» What does heaven mean here? | The sky above the town | *Something very pleasant and delicious | A place with angels and harps | A holy place of God
exercise: «Heaven knows where he put his keys.» What does heaven knows mean? | *Nobody knows | God has written it down | He is very happy | The keys are in the sky
test: «Thank heavens, the rain has stopped!» What does thank heavens show? | Sadness | *Relief | Anger at the rain | Surprise at the sky
test: In old or poetic writing, what does «the heavens» mean? | A cake | *The sky | A holy building | A big house
exam: «Christians believe heaven is being with God for ever, with no more pain or tears.» What does heaven mean here? | *A place where good people are with God after death | A very happy state, like a party | The sky over the town | A name for a cake shop
